  "evidence": "evox17-attempt01 built (exit 0, 1h17m37s) and passed the original verification: archive gate, must-hold (super_empty, fastboot-info and android-info identical to author and build9; DTBO payload and vendor_boot DTB identical to live slot b; 888 modules, 0 CRC mismatches; the one known unresolved symbol; kernel 6.6.142-android15-8-klimt-4k), all 165 historical checks, and all seven supplemental image checks including install_integrity (no stray staged file, image APK set equals the staged set, only the two reviewed evox15 overlay duplicates, TelecomShim is the only com.android.server.telecom APK). Report: C:/XiaomiBuilds/compare/evox17/evox17-attempt01.\n\nThis recheck applies the three verifier gaps found by the independent Codex evox17 review (C:/Users/diogo/Documents/Codex/2026-10-14/ru/work/evox17/codex-review-evox17/EVOX17_FINDINGS.json). None is an image defect; each strengthens a gate:\nE17-001 (high): the Telecom gate trusted the installed path and package name. It now binds the selected Telecom APK to its current producer (module/install/ninja/image byte equality) and classifies the packaged TelecomService binder contract from dexdump (mainline = TelecomServiceInitializerRepository and no ITelecomLoader.Stub subclass). Validated on the real evox16 APKs: Telecom.apk -> legacy, TelecomShim.apk -> mainline; unit tests include a legacy payload at the shim path.\nE17-002 (medium): symlinked APKs skipped identity checks. Installed APK symlinks are now rejected (the evox15, evox16 and evox17 images have none).\nE17-003 (medium): the vendor libdmabufheap was not bound to its producer. libdmabufheap.vendor and libion.vendor are now bound like the system variants (producer/install/image bytes, source edge to BufferAllocator.cpp / ion.c), and libion.vendor's ion_open is checked to be the stub.\nAlso: Check.run decodes tool output with errors='replace' (dexdump of the 2.6 MB legacy Telecom.apk emits non-UTF-8 bytes; without it the checker would crash).\nDry run of all seven modes of the revised checker against the attempt01 extraction: see dryrun results in C:/XiaomiBuilds/debug/evox17/recheck01-dryrun. 45/45 helper and negative tests pass on Linux. Original attempt evidence, extraction and reports are preserved; the recheck uses rechecks/recheck01.",
